  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "When the applied force is fixed, the pressure p (Pa) is inversely proportional to the area S (m²) over which the force acts. When \\(S=0.2\\), \\(p=500\\). Find p when \\(S=0.5\\). (Unit: Pa)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "200",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(p=k/S\\), and \\(k=0.2\\times500=100\\), so \\(p=100/S\\). When \\(S=0.5\\), \\(p=100/0.5=200\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Scale the pressure inversely\n\nThe area increases by a factor of \\(0.5/0.2=5/2\\). For quantities in inverse proportion, multiplying one quantity by a positive factor divides the other by that factor, keeping their product fixed. Thus the pressure becomes\n\\[\np=500\\div\\frac52=500\\times\\frac25=200\\ \\text{Pa}.\n\\]",
